      "body": "Reproduced on main (9.2.0.dev450, Python 3.13): `undo()` raises `AttributeError: 'Config' object has no attribute 'debug'` and the patched value leaks into the next test.\n\nThe `__dict__` lookup added in 0c601d510 assumes that `setattr()` writes into the instance `__dict__`, which is not true when the class defines `__setattr__`. For those objects the old value has to come from `getattr()` and be restored through the same hook, so the old value is wrongly recorded as `NOTSET` and `undo()` tries to delete the attribute.\n\nI'll send a pull request which keeps the `__dict__` lookup for the case it was added for (a plain `object.__setattr__`), with a regression test and a changelog entry.\n\nDisclosure per the project's AI/LLM policy: this is an AI-assisted contribution; the pull request states what was machine-produced and what I verified manually.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
